== Bomb Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Bomb Chest
 | variant = 51
}}

'''Bomb Chests''' (or alternatively '''Stone Chests''') are grey chests that have an appearance similar to stone. They are unique in that they will only open if hit by an explosion. They give the same rewards as Golden Chests. Stone Chests are most commonly found in {{R|Challenge Room}}s, {{R|Curse Room}}s, and {{R|Vault}}s, and they will occasionally replace normal chests.
{{clear}}

== Eternal Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = a
 | name    = Eternal Chest
 | variant = 53
}}

'''Eternal Chests''' are similar in appearance to Golden Chests, except that they are a bright blue instead of gold and emit a pale glow. They have the same requirements to unlock and rewards as locked chests, but with an additional feature: the chest will close itself after a few seconds, at which point it can be opened again for more rewards at the cost of another key. However, there is a 25% chance that the chest will give nothing when opened, and if the chest contains nothing or an item, it will not reclose and cannot give any more rewards. They can be found in {{R|Angel Room}}s, {{R|Vault}}s, and {{R|I AM ERROR}} rooms, and will very rarely replace normal chests and locked chests.

{{dlc|r}}Eternal Chests are guaranteed to pay out at least once.
{{clear}}

== Spiked Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = a
 | name    = Spiked Chest
 | variant = 52
}}

'''Spiked Chests''' are brown-colored chests with spikes protruding from them. Opening the chest will deal half a heart of damage to Isaac unless he has a way to resist the damage, such as with [[invulnerability]] effects or {{i|Holy Mantle}}. {{C|The Forgotten}} can also open spiked chests without taking damage by swinging their bone club. They give the same rewards as normal Chests. They can be rarely found upon completing a room or in Greed mode Shops.

{{dlc|r}} Spiked Chests can also be opened without any damage being taken when using {{I|Magneto}} or holding {{t|Flat File|n}}.

{{dlc|na+}} Unlike other chests, they do not appear on the minimap.
{{clear}}

== Mimic Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc        = a+
 | name       = Mimic Chest
 | image name = {{dlcalt|Mimic Chest|r=Mimic Chest Repentance}}
 | variant    = 54
}}

'''Mimic Chests''' appear similar to normal Chests (both for the sprite and the mini-map icon) until Isaac gets close to them, at which point they sprout spikes and act the same as a Spiked Chest.

{{dlc|nr}} They can be distinguished from normal Chests by their darker, brown coloring, the grayish spots on each side of the latch where the spikes will sprout from, and a tiny bloodstain.

{{dlc|r}} Mimic Chests can be identified through a bloodstain on their bottom-right edge. Damage from this chest is considered self-damage.

The contents inside mimic chests will change whenever their spikes pop out, {{dlc+|r}}which can be observed with {{i|Guppy's Eye}}.{{dlc-}} The only way to get the original drops is to open it with {{t|Flat File}}, {{i|Magneto}}, or a melee swing attack such as {{c|The Forgotten}}'s bone club or {{i|Spirit Sword}}.
{{clear}}

== Old Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = r
 | name    = Old Chest
 | variant = 55
}}

'''Old Chests''' are similar in shape to Golden Chests, but have the color of a normal Chest and a worn-down appearance. They have the same requirements as locked chests. When opened, they contain one of the following:

* 1-3 {{e|Soul Heart}}s (43% chance)
* 3 [[trinket]]s (42% chance)
* An [[Old Chest (Item Pool)|Old Chest item]] (10% chance)
* An [[Angel Room (Item Pool)|Angel Room item]] (5% chance)

Old Chests can be found through the effects of {{I|Isaac's Tomb}} and inside {{R|I AM ERROR}} rooms.
{{clear}}

== Wooden Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Wooden Chest
 | variant     = 56
 | unlocked by = Wooden Chest
}}

'''Wooden Chests''' appear similar to normal Chests, but have a wooden texture. When opened, they contain one of the following:

* 2 [[Cards and Runes|cards or runes]] (45% chance)
* 2-3 [[pill]]s (45% chance)
* A [[Wooden Chest (Item Pool)|Wooden Chest item]] (10% chance)

Wooden Chests have a chance to replace regular chests, and can additionally be found in one {{r|Secret Room}} layout, as well as one {{r|Super Secret Room}} layout. Before they are unlocked, Wooden Chests are replaced by random regular {{E|Chest}}s or {{e|Grab Bag}}s ({{e|Spiked Chest}}s and {{e|Locked Chest}}s cannot replace the regular chest).
{{clear}}

== Mega Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Mega Chest
 | variant     = 57
 | unlocked by = Mega Chest
}}

'''Mega Chests''' appear similar to Golden Chests but are larger in appearance. They require 1-7 keys to open. When opened, they have an equal chance to contain one of the following:

* 2 [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room Items]]
* Pickups equivalent to 5 {{E|Locked Chest}}s, including trinkets, cards, and runes.

Mega Chests have a 0.8328% chance to replace any golden chest, and appears in one super secret room layout next to 2 keys, and one vault room layout. Before they are unlocked, Mega Chests are replaced by {{E|Locked Chest}}s.
{{clear}}

== Haunted Chest ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Haunted Chest
 | variant     = 58
 | unlocked by = Haunted Chest
}}

'''Haunted Chests''' appear nearly identical to normal Chests, but are slightly lighter in color and are haunted by a {{E|Polty}}. A haunted chest deals collision damage while the {{E|Polty}} is inside it. When Isaac gets close enough to a Haunted Chest, the {{E|Polty}} will emerge and throw the chest at him, breaking it open and dealing half a heart of damage if it hits. The {{E|Polty}} then acts normally.
* If the player leaves the room while the chest is in the air, it will disappear.
* If {{E|Polty|text=Polties}} have been permanently destroyed by {{i|Eraser}}, approaching the chest makes it pop open with a pink puff of smoke.
* Using {{i|Pause}} at a time when {{e|Polty}} has not yet picked it up, the chest will be impossible to open in any way until {{e|Polty}} unfreezes or dies. If you try to push {{e|Haunted Chest}} away from {{e|Polty}}, the ghost will appear immediately at the current chest after unfreezing.
{{clear}}

